  "description": "The master of arts in media and strategic communication (MMSC) program provides a unique combination of strategic communication principles, ethics, and creative media production skills for students entering applied communications careers in an era of ever-increasing media convergence. Students can take the program full time in 12 months, or part-time over 2-4 years. Students may apply to the program after successfully completing a four-year degree at an accredited academic institution. A cumulative grade point average of at least 3.0 in the last two years of undergraduate education is required to be admitted to the program. An early-admission, accelerated pathway is available for students currently in one of the undergraduate programs below. Interested students should contact the program advisor for more information. Applied Film and Media Major Digital Communication Film and Media Major: Production Concentration Film and Media Major: Studies Concentration Health Communication Major Sports Communication Major",
